\h Revelation
\toc1 Revelation
\toc2 Revelation
\toc3 Rev.
\mt2 Yohan's
\mt1 Revelation
\mt2 of Yeshua the messiah
\is1 Introduction
\ip \bk Yohan's (John's) revelation of Yeshua (Jesus) the messiah\bk* concerns events that will happen in the future. This was written long ago in a time when the believers were persecuted due to their faith in the master Yeshua, the messiah, and Yohan himself had been forcibly exiled to Patmos Island by the Roman authorities and held there. Yohan's main purpose for writing this was to give hope to the believers and to encourage them to persevere in their faith despite their persecution.
\ip A major portion of what's written in this document is the revelation by Yeshua the messiah to Yohan about incredible signs and all those symbols have a meaning and interpretation. At the time of writing, some were likely understood by the Christians of the time, but now, some of the symbols are very hard to interpret, and there's been a large range of interpretations from different people. But even though it's like that, there are also some signs that are easier to understand like ‘horns’ which denote power and authority, and ‘sword’ which denotes war. The themes are repeated throughout this document in various different forms. But it's important to just understand the main points of what's written here: God will indeed destroy all of his enemies through the messiah Yeshua, and also, he will reward all his people who persevere in serving him, and then he'll bring them to live with him. The final major them concerns the new sky and earth that God will create, and concerning the new Yerushalem that will descend from heaven.
\iot Main components of this document
\io1 Introduction \ior 1:1-8\ior*
\io1 Yohan's first revelation in the form of a dream \ior 1:9-20\ior*
\io1 The letters sent to seven assemblies of believers \ior 2:1–3:22\ior*
\io1 The scroll with seven seals \ior 4:1–8:1\ior*
\io1 The seven trumpets \ior 8:2–11:19\ior*
\io1 The dinosaur and the two creatures \ior 12:1–13:18\ior*
\io1 The various revelations to Yohan as dreams \ior 14:1–15:8\ior*
\io1 The seven bowls of God's anger \ior 16:1-21\ior*
\io1 The destruction of Babylon and the defeat of all God's enemies \ior 17:1–20:10\ior*
\io1 The final judgement \ior 20:11-15\ior*
\io1 The new sky and earth, and the new Yerushalem \ior 21:1–22:5\ior*
\io1 Ending \ior 22:6-21\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\rem /s1 Introduction and Salutation; Prologue
\p
\v 1 \add This is\add* the revelation¦155327 that¦155330 \nd God¦155334\nd* gave¦155331 to \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦155329\nd* to show¦155335 to his slaves¦155338 \add to explain\add* what must happen soon. He communicated it by sending¦155347 it via his messenger¦155350 to his slave¦155354, Yohan¦155357
\v 2 who¦155358 \add then\add* faithfully passed on everything he saw¦155371 of \nd God's\nd* message¦155361 and¦155364 the testimony¦155366 of \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦155368\nd*.
\v 3 \add God will\add* bless anyone who reads or listens to the messages¦155380 of this prophecy¦155384 and¦155385 obeys what's written¦155390 in¦155388 it¦155389, because¦155392 the time¦155393 \add of these events happening\add* is¦155393 close.
\s1 The greetings to seven assemblies of believers
\rem /s1 Christ's messages to seven churches; John's Greeting to the Seven Churches; Greetings to the Seven Churches; Greetings and doxology
\p
\v 4 \add This letter is from\add* Yohan¦155395 to¦155396 the¦155396 seven¦155421 assemblies¦155398 in¦155400 Asia¦155402 \add Minor\add*:\x + \xo 1:4: a \xt Exo 3:14; \xo b \xt Rev 4:5.\x*
\p Grace¦155403 and peace¦155406 to you¦155404 all¦155404 from the \add God\add* who is and was¦155414 and will be, and from the seven spirits¦155422 who are¦155424 in front of¦155429 his¦155429 throne¦155428,
\v 5 and from¦155431 Yeshua \add the\add* \nd messiah¦155433\nd*, the faithful¦155437 witness¦155435, the first¦155439 to come back to life, and the ruler¦155445 of all the leaders \add of the nations\add* of the world.\x + \xo 1:5: a \xt Isa 55:4; \xo b \xt Psa 89:27.\x*
\p \add Yeshua\add* loves¦155452 us and¦155430 he has¦155456 released¦155456 us from our¦155463 sins¦155462 by his¦155467 blood¦155466,
\v 6 and made¦155469 us¦155470 into a kingdom¦155473 of priests¦155476 to \nd God¦155479\nd* his¦155483 father¦155482, and he is deserving of honour and power throughout the ages¦155497. May¦155501 it¦155501 be¦155501 so¦155501.\x + \xo 1:6: \xt Exo 19:6; Rev 5:10.\x*
\p
\v 7 Look¦155502, he's¦155503 going to come¦155503 \add back\add* in the clouds¦155507, and everyone¦155513 will see¦155509 him—the one who¦155516 they¦155518 speared—and all¦155523 the tribes¦155525 on the earth¦155527 will be¦155520 mourning¦155520 over¦155521 him. REWORK OT QUOTES\x + \xo 1:7: a \xt Dan 7:13; Mat 24:30; Mrk 13:26; Luk 21:27; 1Th 4:17; \xo b \xt Zech 12:10; Yhn 19:34,37; \xo c \xt Zech 12:10; Mat 24:30.\x*
\p
\v 8 “I am¦155531 the A and the Z,” says¦155542 \nd Yahweh¦155544 God¦155546\nd*, the one who is and was¦155551 and will be—the most powerful one.\x + \xo 1:8: a \xt Rev 22:13; \xo b \xt Exo 3:14.\x*
\s1 Yohan sees the messiah
\rem /s1 Vision of the Son of Man; A Vision of Christ; One like a Son of Man
\p
\v 9 I, Yohan¦155558, am your¦155562 brother¦155561 and partner in the suffering \add that's typical of those who follow\add* Yeshua. \add I've been exiled to\add* Patmos¦155588 Island¦155585 where I endure¦155574 because¦155589 I believe God's message¦155592 and \nd Yeshua's\nd* testimony¦155598 and \add look forward to\add* his kingdom¦155572.
\v 10 One Sunday \add while I was meditating\add*, \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦155604\nd* gave me a vision, and¦155609 I heard¦155610 a voice¦155614 behind¦155612 me that seemed as loud¦155615 as a trumpet¦155619 blast
\v 11 that said¦155620, “Write¦155637 down what you¦155635 see¦155635 \add here\add* on a scroll¦155640 and send¦155642 it to the seven¦155644 assemblies¦155645 \add of believers\add*—to \add the cities of\add* Ephesus¦155650, Smyrna¦155653, Pergamum¦155656, Thyatira¦155659, Sardis¦155666, Philadelphia¦155669, and to Laodicea¦155672.”
\p
\v 12 Then¦155673 I turned¦155675 to see who was¦155680 talking¦155680 to me¦155684, and¦155673 I saw¦155687 seven¦155688 golden¦155690 lamp holders,
\v 13 and¦155691 standing among them was a man who looked like the son of humanity,\f + \fr 1:13 \ft It's not certain what was meant here: either ‘a man who looked like the son of humanity’ or ‘a form that looked like a human man’.\f* wearing a long robe with a golden¦155711 sash around His¦155702 chest.\x + \xo 1:13: a \xt Dan 7:13; \xo b \xt Dan 10:5.\x*
\v 14 His¦155716 hair¦155719 was gleaming white¦155720 like wool¦155723 or snow¦155726 and¦155714 his¦155716 eyes¦155729 were¦155719 \add bright\add* like a fiery flame¦155732.\x + \xo 1:14: \xt Dan 7:9.\x*
\v 15 His¦155737 feet¦155736 shone like bronze¦155739 that had¦155743 been refined¦155743 in a furnace¦155742, and¦155746 his¦155737 voice¦155748 was like the¦155751 sound of a \add river of rushing\add* water¦155752.\x + \xo 1:15: \xt Eze 1:24; 43:2.\x*
\v 16 He was holding¦155755 seven¦155764 stars¦155763 in¦155757 his right¦155759 hand¦155761 and a sharp¦155772 sword¦155770 was extending from his mouth¦155768, and his face¦155776 was like¦155779 the sun¦155781 shining¦155782 at its¦155786 brightest.
\v 17 And when¦155788 I saw¦155789 him¦155790, I quickly lay at¦155793 his feet¦155795, \add breathless\add* like a dead¦155799 man, but¦155787 he¦155801 placed his right¦155804 hand¦155804 on¦155807 me, and told me, “Don't be¦155812 afraid¦155812. \em I am\em* the first¦155817 and the last.\x + \xo 1:17: \xt Isa 44:6; 48:12; Rev 2:8; 22:13.\x*
\v 18 I lived and died \add here on the earth\add*, but¦155821 look, \add now\add* I'm alive \add again\add* and will live for all eternity, and I control the keys¦155840 over death¦155842 and over hell.
\v 19 So¦155849 record what you're seeing¦155851 \add now\add* as well as \add what I'll show you\add* about current and future events.
\v 20 This is the meaning of the seven stars that¦155870 you¦155871 saw¦155871 in my¦155878 right¦155876 hand¦155876 and of the seven golden¦155884 lamp holders:\x + \xo 1:20: \xt 1:12.\x* The seven stars represent \add God's\add* messengers¦155888 \add watching over\add* those seven groups of believers,\x + \xo 1:20: \xt 1:11.\x* and the seven lamp holders represent those groups of believers.
\c 2
