\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Smyrna
\p
\v 8 To¦156085 the assembly's¦156092 messenger¦156086 in Smyrna¦156090 write¦156094:\x + \xo 2:8: \xt Isa 44:6; 48:12; Rev 1:17; 22:13.\x*
\p The one who's the first¦156099 and¦156084 the last¦156102, who died but¦156084 lived¦156107 \add again\add*, says¦156096 these things:
\v 9 “I know about your suffering and¦156115 your poverty¦156117, but you're¦156121 \add actually\add* rich¦156119! I also know how about the¦156123 slander¦156124 of¦156126 those who consider themselves¦156132 to¦156131 be¦156131 Jews, but they're not \add true\add* Jews because \add ≈their master is\add* Satan¦156139.
\v 10 Don't be afraid¦156142 about what¦156143 you're¦156144 going to suffer¦156146. Yes, the devil¦156153 will throw¦156150 some of¦156154 you into¦156158 prison¦156159 where your¦156154 \add faith\add* will be tested¦156161, and you'll experience persecution for¦156167 ten¦156168 days¦156167. \add Just\add* remain faithful¦156170, even if it means death¦156172, and I'll¦156174 give¦156174 you life¦156179 as a reward.
\p
\v 11 Everyone who wants¦156181 to understand¦156181 needs¦156183 to listen¦156183 to what¦156184 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦156186\nd* is¦156187 saying¦156187 to the¦156188 assemblies¦156189.
\p Anyone who \add stays true\add* won't¦156193 be¦156194 affected by¦156195 the second¦156199 death¦156197.”\x + \xo 2:11: \xt Rev 20:14; 21:8.\x*
\s1 The message to the assembly in Pergamum
\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Pergamum
\p
\v 12 To¦156201 the assembly's¦156206 messenger¦156202 in¦156204 Pergamum¦156205 write¦156207:
\p The one with the sharp¦156217 sword¦156213 says¦156209 these things:
\v 13 “I know¦156218 where you live: where Satan's throne¦156227 is¦156229. Despite that, you firmly \add believe in me\add* and¦156236 you haven't denied your faith¦156240 in me, even when Antipas¦156249, the faithful¦156254 \add man who told others about me\add* was¦156257 killed¦156257 in your \add city\add*, where Satan lives.
\v 14 But¦156296 I do have a few things against¦156267 you: you have some¦156271 people there¦156273 who¦156278 hold¦156274 to \add the ancient prophet\add* Balaam's teaching.\x + \xo 2:14: a \xt Num 22:5,7; 31:16; Deu 23:4; \xo b \xt Num 25:1-3.\x* He taught¦156276 \add Moab's king\add*, Balak¦156284, how to tempt¦156288 the Israelis and to eat¦156294 \add food\add* that had been sacrificed¦156295 to idols, and to be sexually¦156297 immoral¦156297.
\v 15 In the same way, some¦156299 of you¦156301 also follow the teachings¦156304 of Nicolaus' disciples.\f + \fr 2:15 \ft They eat food that has been sacrificed to idols, and they commit sexual sins.\f*
\v 16 So¦156313 turn away from all that, otherwise I'll¦156320 come¦156315 soon and¦156319 battle against them¦156322 with¦156323 the word of my¦156328 mouth¦156327.
\p
\v 17 Everyone¦156363 who wants¦156330 to understand¦156330 needs¦156332 to listen¦156332 to what¦156333 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦156335\nd* is¦156336 saying¦156336 to the¦156368 assemblies¦156338.
\p Anyone¦156363 who \add stays true\add* will¦156341 be¦156341 given hidden¦156349 food from heaven, and¦156355 I'll¦156341 give \add each of\add* them a white¦156354 stone¦156353 with a new¦156360 name¦156359 written¦156361 on¦156356 it that¦156348 no¦156363 one¦156363 knows¦156364 apart from the person receiving¦156369 it.”\x + \xo 2:17: a \xt Exo 16:14-15; 16:33-34; Yhn 6:48-50; \xo b \xt Isa 62:2; 65:15.\x*
\s1 The message to the assembly in Thyatira
\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Thyatira
\p
\v 18 To¦156371 the assembly's¦156377 messenger¦156372 in¦156375 Thyatira¦156376 write¦156378:
\p God's son¦156382, the one with eyes¦156388 like a flame¦156391 of fire¦156393 and¦156394 with feet¦156396 like bronze¦156399, says¦156380:
\v 19 “I know¦156400 what you've been doing, and \add about\add* your love¦156406 and faith¦156409, and your service¦156413 and endurance¦156417, and what you're doing now is better than what you first¦156428 did.
\v 20 But¦156453 I have¦156430 against¦156431 you that you tolerate that woman Jezebel¦156442 who calls¦156446 herself¦156448 a prophetess¦156451, and she¦156454 deceives my¦156460 servants by teaching¦156454 them to be sexually¦156462 immoral¦156462 and to eat¦156464 \add food that's been\add* offered to idols.\x + \xo 2:20: \xt 1Ki 16:31; 2Ki 9:22,30.\x*
\v 21 Even though I've given her time¦156470 to repent, she's \add still\add* not willing to turn away from her immorality¦156480.
\v 22 Listen, I'm going to \add punish her with a terrible sickness\add*, and¦156494 to punish those who are committing¦156496 adultery¦156496 with her with terrible suffering if¦156502 they¦156505 don't¦156503 turn away from what she's doing.
\v 23 I will kill¦156515 her¦156514 children¦156513, then¦156511 all¦156520 the assemblies¦156522 will know¦156519 that¦156523 I am¦156525 the one who searches¦156527 \add people's\add* affections and hearts¦156530, and who \add punishes or rewards\add* each¦156534 one of¦156538 you¦156538 depending on your¦156538 actions.\x + \xo 2:23: a \xt Psa 7:9; Jer 17:10; \xo b \xt Psa 62:12.\x*
\p
\v 24 But the rest¦156545 of you \add believers in the city\add* of Thyatira¦156548 haven't obeyed that woman's teachings¦156553 and haven't taken part in what she calls ‘the secret practices that Satan¦156563 taught¦156553 her’, I have¦156551 something to say to you¦156539 all¦156539 as¦156564 well. I won't¦156550 give you any other other burden¦156572
\v 25 except just to continue to obey the true teaching that¦156579 you've received, until¦156578 I return.
\v 26 And¦156585 anyone who's victorious, who continues to do what I command until¦156588 the end¦156589, I'll¦156593 give¦156593 them authority¦156595 to rule over¦156596 the people groups on earth.\x + \xo 2:26-27: \xt Psa 2:8-9 (LXX).\x*
\v 27 They'll rule them with irresistible power, and¦156599 \add those who rebel\add* will be smashed like \add unwanted\add* clay pots,
\v 28 just like \add the authority\add* that I've¦156614 received¦156615 from my¦156619 father¦156618. And¦156620 I'll¦156621 give¦156621 them the morning¦156626 star¦156624.
\p
\v 29 Everyone who wants¦156628 to understand¦156628 needs¦156630 to listen¦156630 to what¦156631 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦156633\nd* is¦156634 saying¦156634 to the¦156635 assemblies¦156636.”
\c 3
\s1 The message to the assembly in Sardis
\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Sardis
\p
\v 1 To¦156638 the¦156650 assembly's¦156643 messenger¦156639 in¦156641 Sardis¦156642 write¦156645:
\p The¦156648 one having¦156649 the seven spirits¦156652 of \nd God¦156654\nd* and the seven stars¦156658 says¦156647 these things: “I know¦156659 what you're achieving and that you have¦156659 a reputation¦156665 of being ‘alive’, but¦156637 you're \add actually\add* dead¦156670.
\v 2 So wake up \add from the dead\add* and strengthen¦156675 what's left and was about to¦156683 die¦156683, because¦156685 your¦156687 actions have¦156686 been¦156690 inadequate in God's sight.
\v 3 Remember¦156695 how you \add first\add* listened to and internalised \add God's message\add*, and how you obeyed it¦156702 and repented¦156704. If¦156706 you don't¦156708 wake up \add soon\add*, I'll come \add unexpectedly\add*—you'll certainly not¦156718 know¦156719 \add in advance\add* when I'll be¦156724 coming.\x + \xo 3:3: \xt Mat 24:43-44; Luk 12:39-40; Rev 16:15.\x*
\v 4 But¦156742 you¦156728 do have¦156728 a few¦156729 people in Sardis¦156734 who¦156735 haven't stained their¦156741 records, and because¦156750 they are worthy¦156751, they'll \add be\add* dressed in white¦156749 and walk¦156743 with¦156746 me¦156747.
\v 5 \add So\add* anyone who conquers will¦156757 be¦156757 dressed like that in¦156759 \add pure\add* white¦156761, and I certainly won't¦156764 erase their names from¦156769 the Book of Life¦156773, but¦156762 I'll¦156765 declare their names to my¦156784 father¦156783 and to his¦156768 messengers¦156788.\x + \xo 3:5: a \xt Exo 32:32-33; Psa 69:28; Rev 20:12; \xo b \xt Mat 10:32; Luk 12:8.\x*
\p
\v 6 Everyone who wants¦156791 to understand¦156791 needs¦156793 to listen¦156793 to what¦156794 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦156796\nd* is¦156797 saying¦156797 to the¦156798 assemblies¦156799.”
\s1 The message to the assembly in Filadelfia
\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Philadelphia
\p
\v 7 To¦156801 the¦156812 assembly's¦156807 messenger¦156802 in Filadelfia¦156805 write¦156809:\x + \xo 3:7: \xt Isa 22:22; Yob 12:14.\x*
\p The holy¦156813 one, the true¦156815 one, the one having¦156819 \add King\add* David's key¦156821 \add to the city\add*, the one who opens \add doors\add* no one can shut, and¦156800 who shuts \add doors\add* no one can open, says¦156811:
\v 8 “I know \add everything\add* you've been¦156855 doing. Listen¦156850, I have¦156845 placed an opened¦156855 door¦156854 in front of¦156846 you that¦156856 no¦156858 one¦156858 can shut¦156862. You¦156866 aren't¦156874 very strong, yet¦156868 you've obeyed my¦156870 instructions and¦156873 you haven't disowned¦156875 knowing¦156845 me¦156878.
\v 9 Listen¦156879, I'll give¦156882 those¦156882 \add people\add* from Satan's¦156887 synagogue¦156885 (the ones who say¦156889 that they're \add believing\add* Jews, but¦156893 they're not—they're lying¦156897), I'll make¦156899 them¦156900 so that they will¦156903 come¦156903 and bow down in front of¦156910 you, and \add then\add* they'll know¦156912 that I love¦156916 you.\x + \xo 3:9: a \xt Isa 49:23; 60:14; \xo b \xt Isa 43:4.\x*
\v 10 Because¦156919 you followed my¦156926 instructions about persevering, I will spare you from the time of trouble that¦156935 all of humanity will soon experience (which¦156935 will test¦156942 everyone living¦156945 on the earth¦156948).
\v 11 I'll come¦156950 quickly¦156951. Hold¦156952 firmly to what¦156953 you¦156954 have¦156954 so that¦156955 no¦156956 one¦156956 can take¦156957 away your¦156960 crown¦156959.
\v 12 Anyone who's an overcomer¦156962, I'll¦156963 make¦156963 them a pillar¦156966 in¦156967 my god's temple¦156969 and they'll never leave it again. I will write¦156981 my god's name on them, and the name of my god's city¦156993 (the new Jerusalem which will come¦156978 down¦157002 out¦157003 of heaven¦157005 from¦157006 my god), and my new name.\x + \xo 3:12: a \xt Rev 21:2; \xo b \xt Isa 62:2; 65:15.\x*
\p
\v 13 Everyone who wants¦157017 to understand¦157017 needs¦157019 to listen¦157019 to what¦157020 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦157022\nd* is¦157023 saying¦157023 to the¦157024 assemblies¦157025.”
\s1 The message to the assembly in Laodicea
\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Laodicea
\p
\v 14 To¦157027 the assembly's¦157032 messenger¦157028 in¦157030 Laodicea¦157031 write¦157034:\x + \xo 3:14: \xt Prv 8:22.\x*
\p The truth, the faithful¦157043 and¦157044 true¦157046 witness¦157041, the originator of¦157050 God's creation¦157052, says¦157036:
\v 15 “I'm aware of what you've been doing \add and\add* that¦157059 you're¦157062 neither¦157060 hot nor cold. (You'd benefit\f + \fr 3:15 \ft TC: Some manuscripts don't have this parenthesised sentence at all, and some later manuscripts have ‘I wish’ instead of ‘You'd benefit’.\f* if you were¦157068 hot or cold.)
\v 16 So because¦157073 you're¦157076 lukewarm¦157075, neither¦157078 hot¦157080 nor¦157082 cold¦157083, I'll spit¦157089 you out¦157090 of my¦157094 mouth¦157092.
\v 17 You¦157096 brag, ‘I'm rich, \add yes\add* I've¦157101 grown rich and don't have any needs,’ but¦157100 you don't realise that you're¦157096 \add actually\add* miserable¦157114 and pitiable, and poor¦157120 and blind¦157122 and naked¦157124.
\v 18 I advise you to buy gold¦157131 from¦157129 me¦157130 that's been¦157132 refined¦157132 by¦157133 fire¦157134 so that you might get rich¦157136, and buy white¦157139 clothes¦157138 so that you can dress yourself¦157141 so that the shame¦157146 of your nakedness¦157148 might not be displayed, and buy ointment to rub¦157153 on your eyes¦157157 so that you'll be able to see¦157160.
\v 19 I tell off and discipline¦157168 those that I love¦157165, so be¦157170 earnest and turn away from your disobedience.\x + \xo 3:19: \xt Prv 3:12; Heb 12:6.\x*
\v 20 Yes, I stand¦157175 at¦157176 the door and knock¦157180—if anyone¦157182 hears¦157183 my¦157186 voice¦157185 and opens¦157188 the door, I will¦157193 come¦157193 in¦157193 and eat with him¦157199, and he'll eat with me¦157203.
